      "narration": "Remember that crime chart? The axis starting at 98.2 was the whole trick. Once you saw where the ruler began, the dramatic cliff shrank back into a small wobble. And the toothpaste ad was the same trick wearing a different outfit.\n\nSo here's a little checklist you can carry around. First: what does the axis start at? Second: percent of what? Third: compared to what? Three questions, and they'll catch a surprising number of bad charts.\n\nBut all of this is only a high-level view, just a peek at how numbers get bent. I haven't touched cherry-picked dates, or the whole mess of correlation versus causation. That's the next video.\n\nUntil then, here's a small exercise. This week, find one misleading chart in your feed. Ask the three questions. I think you'll be a little annoyed at how quickly you spot it.",
